---
description: Type discipline — no any, no un-narrowed unknown. Escape hatches are design bugs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Types

Silent on untyped files (Bash, JSON, CSS, Markdown). On typed languages: fix the design; don't silence the compiler.

- No `any`.
- No `unknown` as a public signature, return type, or stored field. Catch / JSON / IO may bind `unknown` only if the next statements narrow it before it is used or passed on.
- No blind casts, unwrap, or ignored errors.
- Do not add suppressions just to pass CI (`@ts-ignore`, `# type: ignore` without a one-line why).
- Prefer: sum types over parallel booleans; the repo's fallible-op idiom; explicit public signatures; schema-inferred types when schemas exist; one nullish convention per repo.

Escape hatch = design bug.
